---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="Self-host — The Relic" description="Run The Relic entirely on your own infrastructure. Free, open source, no telemetry.">
  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-white/5">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-6">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <a href="/" class="text-xl font-bold text-white">The Relic</a>
          <nav class="flex items-center gap-6">
            <a href="/" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Home</a>
            <a href="/self-host" class="text-sm font-medium text-relic-400">Self-host</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/therelicai/therelic" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">GitHub</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-relic-400">Self-host</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
          Run the whole stack on your own infrastructure.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-neutral-400">
          The Relic is free and open source. You bring your own Postgres + S3-compatible
          storage (MinIO works locally); everything else is shipped as static binaries
          and small Go services. No SaaS dependency. No telemetry.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Layout overview -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What you're running</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Runtime</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">relic CLI</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              A single Go binary that wraps any agent process, enforces policy, and writes
              tamper-evident NDJSON traces. Runs on the same machine as the agent.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-neutral-500">Apache 2.0</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Control plane</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">relic-api</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              Go service that indexes uploaded traces, verifies their HMAC chains, and
              exposes a REST API. Backed by Postgres + S3.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-neutral-500">BSL 1.1 → Apache 2.0 after change date</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Dashboard</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">therelic-app</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              React + Vite SPA. Reads from relic-api. View runs, replay actions, manage
              policies, review proposals. Ships as static assets you can host anywhere.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-neutral-500">BSL 1.1 → Apache 2.0 after change date</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Quickstart -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 bg-neutral-950 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Quickstart</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-neutral-400">
          Three steps. The control plane runs out of one <code class="rounded bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-relic-400">docker compose up</code>;
          the runtime is a single binary.
        </p>

        <ol class="mt-10 space-y-10">
          <li>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Step 1</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold text-white">Install the runtime</p>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-black px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-300">
              <p><span class="text-neutral-600">#</span> macOS / Linux via Homebrew</p>
              <p>brew install therelicai/tap/relic</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-neutral-600"># Or build from source</p>
              <p>go install github.com/therelicai/therelic/cmd/relic@latest</p>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Step 2</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold text-white">Bring up the control plane</p>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-black px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-300">
              <p>git clone https://github.com/therelicai/therelic-platform</p>
              <p>cd therelic-platform</p>
              <p>docker compose up -d   <span class="text-neutral-600"># postgres, minio, relic-api</span></p>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-500">
              Defaults bind to <code class="rounded bg-white/5 px-1 text-xs text-relic-400">localhost:8080</code> for the API
              and <code class="rounded bg-white/5 px-1 text-xs text-relic-400">localhost:9001</code> for the MinIO console.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">Step 3</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold text-white">Wrap your first agent</p>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-black px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-300">
              <p>relic init</p>
              <p>export RELIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080</p>
              <p>export RELIC_API_KEY=$(relic auth issue --org dev)</p>
              <p>relic run -- python my_agent.py</p>
              <p>relic trace push     <span class="text-neutral-600"># push the trace to the dashboard</span></p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-neutral-500">
          See the full self-host guide in
          <a href="https://github.com/therelicai/therelic-platform#self-host" class="text-relic-400 underline hover:text-white">
            therelic-platform/README
          </a>, including hardening (HMAC trace key, JWT issuer pinning, RLS) and air-gapped install.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What's free / what's not -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">No paywall. No gated features.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-neutral-400">
          When you self-host The Relic, you get everything: the policy engine, the
          exfiltration guard, the trace HMAC chain, the dashboard, audit logs, the
          retention worker, all of it. There is no "team tier" or "enterprise tier"
          locked behind a Stripe checkout — that was the old plan, and it isn't the
          plan anymore.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-neutral-400">
          The runtime is Apache 2.0. The control plane and dashboard are BSL 1.1, which
          means you can run them in production, in your own VPC, for your own users, for
          free — the only thing the license restricts is selling them as a managed
          service of your own, and after the change date they automatically convert to
          Apache 2.0.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="border-t border-white/5 py-12">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-6 sm:flex-row">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
            <a href="/" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Home</a>
            <a href="/self-host" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Self-host</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/therelicai/therelic" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">GitHub</a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500">© {new Date().getFullYear()} The Relic. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
